  You had most of the right ideas.  You just tried to do all of 
them at once, guaranteeing that none of them would work.

  All mind flayers are speed 12, the same as a slow human.  
Running should pretty much always work if the (m)mf isn't too 
close (i.e. two or fewer squares away.)


  If you see a (m)mf in the distance, don't let it get within
three squares of you.  Start running first.  Try to find some
way of blocking the flayer's advance: boulder, trap, dust 
Elbereth, etc.

  Elbereth is for when you can't run.  (NB: It's easier to run 
when a monster is moving more randomly due to being scared by 
Elbereth.)

  A couple of good Elbereths in the dust are almost guaranteed
to work, IF you're not too active on top of them.

  Since you were in a corridor, you had it made:
    - Write a couple of good dust Elbereths 
    - Drop an item on them
    - Optionally check the engraving
    - Then step back
    - Repeat the process a few times for peace of mind.
    - Hostiles afraid of Elbereth will not step on an Elbereth 
      square with an object on it.

  - No mind flayers are sleep resistant.  Since you had arrows, a
mindflayer hit with a wand of sleep should be no threat at all.
So start out with the wand of sleep until the mind flayer is 
anesthetized, or you feel like it's time to RUN!  

  It is much, much better to hit the flayer with the wand of 
sleep than a few arrows.  A hit with the wand of sleep should
have let you use your arrows (or even just rocks) safely.

